  "termination": "completed",
  "answer": "I fixed the shared parser state machine in `src/state.mjs` (and aligned `src/line.mjs`). I could not run tests (no execution tool available), so nothing is claimed as passing.\n\nWhat was wrong and what changed:\n\n- **Doubled quotes across chunks** (`src/state.mjs`): in `afterQuote` mode, a second `\"` previously threw `INVALID_QUOTE`. Now `\"\"` appends one literal `\"` and returns to `quoted` mode, so `\"say \"\"hi\"\"\"` unescapes correctly regardless of where the chunk boundary falls.\n- **CRLF split across chunks**: a `\\r` outside quotes now sets `pendingCR` and defers the decision to the next character (or end of input). The next char must be `\\n` (record ends) or it throws `BARE_CR`; a trailing `\\r` at end of input throws `BARE_CR` in `finishState`. This makes `['a,one\\r', '\\nb,two']` and `['a,one\\r\\nb,two']` identical.\n- **Record ending after a closing quote**: `afterQuote` now handles `\\n` and `\\r` (via `pendingCR`) as valid record terminators, and `endRecord` resets `mode`/`atFieldStart`/`pendingCR` so state is clean for the next record.\n- **`src/line.mjs`**: `consumeLine` no longer treats a bare `\\r` as a record terminator; it only ends a record on `\\n` (CRLF is handled by the pending-CR logic in the state machine).\n\nUnchanged: `parseRows`, `readItems`, `countItems` exports and their signatures; `parseRows` still throws `TypeError` for non-array input and for non-string chunks (via `tokenizer.push`); consumers still share `parseRows` and `validateItemRow`, so both see identical records and errors; slug/checksum helpers untouched; public tests untouched.\n\nBehavior preserved per spec: empty input → `[]`/`0`, blank line → `['']`, trailing line ending adds no extra record, final unterminated record included, fields not trimmed, quoted CRLF preserved literally, and error codes `INVALID_QUOTE`/`UNTERMINATED_QUOTE`/`BARE_CR`/`COLUMN_COUNT`/`EMPTY_ID` unchanged.",
